{
  "_comment": [
    "What the shipping app actually loads, with the hashes to prove a re-download is the",
    "same file. Rewritten 2026-08-08: every previous entry had an empty url and sha256 at",
    "status 'pending-selfhost', so `make bootstrap` printed '0 fetched, 4 skipped' and",
    "exited 0 — a green run that downloaded nothing, for models the app does not use.",
    "A command that succeeds without doing anything is worse than no command.",
    "Hashes below were taken from the working copies on 2026-08-08 and match the official",
    "Hugging Face repo byte for byte. See docs/RECOVERY.md.",
    "2026-09-29 (C2): uzbek_stt_v1 added — it had been what the app loads since D-08 while the manifest still listed only navoi-medium.",
    "`bundles` are Core ML models: directories pinned file by file to one Hugging Face commit. Generated by Scripts/measure/en-ru/hf_manifest.py; ModelCatalogue mirrors them and ModelCatalogueManifestTests asserts the two agree.",
    "2026-09-30 (C2): navoi-medium removed — superseded by D-08 and not shipped; the Uzbek engine now resolves through public_models_base."
  ],
  "public_models_base": "https://github.com/aziznizomofficial/kotiba/releases/download/models-v2/",
  "_public_models_base": "THE ONE PLACE this project's own model builds are published for strangers: release models-v2 of aziznizomofficial/kotiba (uploaded 2026-10-01 for 1.0.0). GitHub 404s release assets of a private repo to a plain GET, so while the repository is private fetch-models.py takes the entry's `release` route (the same asset) through gh. Every entry with `public_asset` is fetched from public_models_base + public_asset; change owner/repo/tag here (and in ModelCatalogue.publicModelsBase and windows/src/contracts/models.ts PUBLIC_MODELS_BASE — tests assert all three agree) when the host is live. If the plain GET fails, fetch-models.py falls back to the entry's `release` route through gh.",
